# ── secrets. nothing here is recoverable once it is public. ──────────────────────
keys/
.npmrc
*.pem
*.key

# publish.js writes .npmrc containing the registry auth token and removes it in a `finally`.
# A killed process skips `finally`, leaving the token sitting in the working tree. The whole
# point of an automation token is that it publishes with no human in the loop — so a leaked
# one is a stranger shipping code under my name. Ignored belt-and-braces.

# ── build artefacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
*.tgz

# ── local hook state, not source ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.claude/hooks/.signals.offset
.claude/hooks/.last-fired.json
*.spine-backup-*

# ── mine, not the customer's ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# internal playbook, fulfilment tooling, release pipeline. gitignore has no inline
# comments — a trailing # makes it match a filename containing that comment, so these
# patterns sat here doing nothing while the files stayed untracked-but-shippable.
outreach.md
sign-license.js
publish.js
golive.js
